<sn><md>### Structure of an Ecosystem

The structure of an ecosystem is basically a description of the `organisms and physical features` of the environment including the `amount and distribution of nutrients` in a particular habitat. It also provides information regarding the range of climatic conditions prevailing in the area.

From the structure point of view, all ecosystems consist of two main components:

1. `Abiotic` component
2. `Biotic` component
